{
  "id": "18851_zousetsu",
  "headword": "{増設|ぞうせつ}",
  "reading": "ぞうせつ",
  "romaji": "zousetsu",
  "part_of_speech": "noun",
  "gloss": "expansion; addition; installation of more",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "suru",
    "prefix": "{増設|ぞうせつ}"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "expansion; addition; installation of more",
      "explanation": "Adding more of something that already exists — more facilities, equipment, lines, or capacity to an existing system or structure."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "18851_zousetsu_ex1",
      "japanese": "メモリーを{増設|ぞうせつ}する。",
      "english": "I'll add more memory.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18851_zousetsu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{駐車場|ちゅうしゃじょう}を{増設|ぞうせつ}する{計画|けいかく}がある。",
      "english": "There is a plan to add more parking spaces.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18851_zousetsu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{利用者|りようしゃ}の{増加|ぞうか}に{対応|たいおう}するため、{窓口|まどぐち}を{二|ふた}つ{増設|ぞうせつ}した。",
      "english": "Two more service counters were added to accommodate the increase in users.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Used as both a noun and a suru-verb ({増設|ぞうせつ}する). The key nuance is adding more of something that already exists, not building something new from scratch. Common objects include {設備|せつび} (equipment/facilities), メモリー (computer memory), {教室|きょうしつ} (classrooms), and {路線|ろせん} (routes/lines). Contrasts with {新設|しんせつ} (newly establishing something that didn't exist before).",
